Katemark for Sparky Stereo OS
-----------------------------

The plugin is installed and off. In Kate: Settings, Configure Kate, Plugins, tick Katemark, OK. Ctrl+Shift+M opens
and closes the preview beside the document.

Nothing is fetched from the network by default. Katemark's own page of Kate's settings has two choices that can reach it:
"Load media previews from remote URLs" (off) lets a picture on the web load into the preview, and "Check for updates"
asks GitHub for the latest release only when the button is clicked. The package manager keeps this package up to date;
the button's answer is about upstream's releases, not about this package.

The JavaScript libraries (markdown-it and its plugins, KaTeX, Mermaid, highlight.js, js-yaml) are upstream's bundled
minified copies, compiled into the plugin; their versions and licences are in debian/copyright and in
/usr/share/doc/katemark/THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md. Debian's copies are older (KaTeX 0.16.10 against the bundled 0.19.0,
Mermaid 9.2.2 against 12.1.0, highlight.js 10.7.3 against 11.10.0) and upstream tests only the bundled ones.
